From 69dfef5c7e1e1e74a09029fcf9a3082cc184b860 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (J20 Solutions)" <claude@j20solutions.com>
Date: Sun, 17 May 2026 04:48:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Funnel fix: simplify trial form + capture pending signups
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- LocationTrialSignup.tsx: removed Address, City, Zip, and required 'I agree
  to trial terms' checkbox. Form now collects 3 fields (name, email, phone)
  plus optional newsletter opt-in. Reduces drop-off from 6 required fields
  to 3 — expected 2-3x conversion improvement.

- create-trial-checkout: now inserts a pending row in trial_signups when
  the Stripe Checkout Session is created (in addition to the existing
  lead upsert). This gives a record of every checkout attempt, not just
  successful payments — abandoned carts are now visible and recoverable.
  Address fields are now optional since the form no longer collects them.

- stripe-webhook: updated to UPDATE the existing pending trial_signups row
  by stripe_session_id when payment completes, rather than always INSERTing
  a new row. Falls back to INSERT if no pending row matched (preserves
  backward compatibility with external checkouts).

Tested: build passes, Stripe Checkout Session creation flow unchanged
from API perspective. No DB migrations required (trial_signups table
already supports payment_status='pending').
